+# Full independent review request: 30004047
+
+Proposed original disposition: unsolved 5/5. Please audit the full exact source and all five proofs, rather than accepting partials as the bundled source answer. Both the one-third diagonal assertion and the unrestricted asymmetric integer-k implication remain unresolved.
+
+Read SOURCE_SCOPE.md, RESULT.md, then TURN_1 through TURN_5. The original Seymour contribution is OWR1/2019 printed46--47/PDF42--43. The published 2022 paper supplies definitions, weighted framework, phi symmetry, Conjecture5.1 and the credited existing lower bounds. The neighboring psi-symmetry PR364 is distinct; it is not a proof dependency for any new theorem here.
+
+Highest-risk obligations:
+
+- exact universal-over-finite-graphs quantifiers, distinct vertices rather than path multiplicity, and absence of the two reverse degree constraints;
+- fixed-template LP quantifiers and the difference between its value and unrestricted phi;
+- the complete-uniform family evaluation and its all-k no-counterexample inequalities;
+- weighted rank-two support, the half-integral five-vertex cover lemma, and the incompatible-type C-disjointness argument;
+- maximal-type count and charge, especially strict y>1/(k+1), ordinary/uniform A, and the nonmonotone cardinality regimes;
+- the n=4k+1 residual-space argument, classification of residual triples, exceptional charge case, and distinction between contained and residual middle types;
+- the unbounded disjoint-maximal theorem with full asymmetric endpoints, deletion stability, and the precise scope of the local uncrossing failure;
+- every failed-mechanism example being kept separate from an original counterexample.
+
+Replay the exact checkers and verify all historical/source bindings. The finite checks support rather than establish the infinite scope of the analytic theorems. Any necessary correction must be additive to frozen historical files. No sixth author proof-search turn is available.
