+2026-10-02 18:56 UTC: Proved a weighted rank-two incidence theorem by combining a five-vertex half-integral fractional-cover lemma with disjoint last-neighborhood certificates. Below-half reach forces x<=2/5; if x>1/3 it also forces y<=1/4. A 14-vertex endpoint example and an ordinary |A|<=6 corollary retain exact scope. All 20,643 finite controls pass. Original unresolved, 2/5; higher-rank middle neighborhoods remain. Subjective completion estimate 20%.
