+
+2026-10-02 19:05 UTC: Proved maximal-type count t<=k-1 under y>1/(k+1), then an explicit dual charge. The symmetric threshold is established for ordinary |A|<=4k, so a diagonal half-reach counterexample needs at least nine first vertices. A nine-vertex first-incidence relaxation attains the charge bound but cannot meet the C-degree condition; this failure is proved explicitly. All 12,105,108 finite arithmetic controls pass. Original unresolved, 3/5; subjective completion 25%.
